{"id":"u-cffe4b42-3c75-4cb0-a18f-88a94dcbebfd","src":"community","title":"Dr. Mike’s Superman Aesthetics Program","author":"Matt D.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/toFp8D-dr-mikes-superman-aesthetics-program","desc":"This plan prioritizes shape over symmetry. To emulate Superman’s iconic frame, three muscle groups take precedence:\n\nUpper Pecs: Provide depth and posture, especially visible in fitted clothing or side profiles.\n\nLateral Delts: Expand shoulder width dramatically, creating that broad-shouldered look from every angle.\n\nLats and Upper Back: Deliver the V-taper, a hallmark of power and aesthetic size.\n\nWhile arms and legs are trained, they’re purposefully deprioritized to reduce fatigue and emphasize upper body growth where it matters most.\n\nThe program uses a five-day structure, rotating muscle group priority to balance recovery and intensity. This rotation ensures that each of the three target muscle groups has a chance to be trained first, when you're freshest, increasing quality volume and long-term growth potential.\n\nExercise Selection, Sets, and Reps:\nEach main day includes 5 movements total. Start with 2 sets per exercise, progressing based on recovery and soreness. Add 1 rep each week until you reach the end of the rep range. Then, add 5lbs and begin again. After 4–8 weeks of progression, schedule a deload: train only twice that week, cut reps, sets, and weight by 50%, and allow fatigue to dissipate.\n\nThis isn’t a general fitness plan. It’s a physique-forward hypertrophy program built to exaggerate the exact muscles that give the illusion of superhuman power. After 8–16 weeks, expect visual changes — broader shoulders, fuller chest, and back width that commands space. Repeat it with new variations or shift to another aesthetic goal, but the blueprint here remains a reliable foundation for building the kind of physique that turns heads — or at least earns a nod from Lois Lane.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":11,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-20T12:09:45.281Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chest, Delts, Back","Legs & Arms","Back, Chest, Delts","Arms & Legs","Delts, Back, Chest"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Upright Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"High Row","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Good Morning","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Skull Crusher (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Assisted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Upright Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Upright Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Straight Arm Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9